<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#early-bronze-age">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Early Bronze Age</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 3300–2000 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> is the first phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze</a> Age in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>, roughly 3300 to 2000 BCE. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> it saw the first walled towns, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-megiddo">Megiddo</a>; in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, sites like Tiryns and Orchomenos grew into substantial settlements with large central buildings, long before the Mycenaean palaces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/early-bronze-age.jpg" alt="Early Bronze Age" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Want · CC BY-SA 3.0 cz · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metallurgical_diffusion.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
